# Jak II: each kind of settings row by the pointer (LIST-0.1.3 item 1), with JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1, on the settings copy
# C:\JakQuest\sim\gkcfg-ptrset (it changes them, then changes them back). The title's menu as jak2_ptr_scroll.sim (the
# dot on Options at 10 degrees, the trigger; on the Options menu's first row at 20, the trigger: Game Options). Jak II's
# pages (4:3) show 5 rows of 40 from y 112 of the 416-high screen: pitch 24.1, 19.5, 14.6, 9.45, 4.2 (pitch
# atan((0.35 + (0.5 - y / 416) * 1.26) / 1.3)); a row is 40 to 472 across: its middle yaw 8.75, its left third (x 110)
# 27.6, its right third (x 400) -11.8. A row being changed takes a click on its left or right third as a step that way
# (held: again every 0.09 s after 0.4 s), in its middle as done (pc-vr.gc vr-ptr-zone-click!).
# - Subtitles (On / Off, the third row): the dot onto it, a click (being changed), a click on the right third, on the
#   left third (back), in the middle (done).
# - The stick down three rows (the page moves on one), the dot onto Subtitle Language (now the fourth row shown): the
#   same clicks.
# - B back, the stick down to Sound Options, A; the second row (a volume): a click, the trigger held 70 frames on the
#   right third (up some steps), then 70 on the left third (back down), a click in the middle (done). B back.
